{
  "schema_version": "argument_graph/0.1",
  "example_id": "persuade:AD0F893FA473",
  "root": "u1",
  "units": [
    {
      "id": "u1",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 73,
      "text": "We shouldn't have Electoral College for many reasons but a few main ones.",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u2",
      "start": 74,
      "end": 108,
      "text": "First off it isn't fiar to voters,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u3",
      "start": 109,
      "end": 137,
      "text": "secondly it may cause riots,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u4",
      "start": 138,
      "end": 165,
      "text": "and finally they are basis.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u5",
      "start": 167,
      "end": 199,
      "text": "If we continue Electoral College",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u6",
      "start": 200,
      "end": 253,
      "text": "it is not going to give the votes a chance to be seen",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u7",
      "start": 254,
      "end": 282,
      "text": "because the college can vote",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u8",
      "start": 283,
      "end": 342,
      "text": "but the Electoral College is the main vote the country sees",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u9",
      "start": 343,
      "end": 381,
      "text": "because the country always miss counts",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u10",
      "start": 382,
      "end": 407,
      "text": "and have a smaller number",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u11",
      "start": 408,
      "end": 426,
      "text": "if they miss count",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u12",
      "start": 427,
      "end": 507,
      "text": "the percentage of votes can be impacted a lot more and with the 60 percent rule.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u13",
      "start": 508,
      "end": 565,
      "text": "and yes the College style of votining is used a lot today",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u14",
      "start": 566,
      "end": 594,
      "text": "if we use one vote per state",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u15",
      "start": 595,
      "end": 622,
      "text": "you see how you state votes",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u16",
      "start": 623,
      "end": 656,
      "text": "and dont have to demand a recount",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u17",
      "start": 657,
      "end": 706,
      "text": "because it was already counted for at state level",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u18",
      "start": 707,
      "end": 741,
      "text": "and isn't needed at national level",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u19",
      "start": 742,
      "end": 790,
      "text": "so we wont have a hard time counting everything.",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u20",
      "start": 792,
      "end": 845,
      "text": "This method of voting useing a few people to vote for",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u21",
      "start": 847,
      "end": 851,
      "text": "\"our",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u22",
      "start": 853,
      "end": 911,
      "text": "\" president is not the smartest thing the country has done",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u23",
      "start": 912,
      "end": 955,
      "text": "and they prove to be wrong every four years",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u24",
      "start": 956,
      "end": 998,
      "text": "becuse the amoust of prosteting will go up",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u25",
      "start": 999,
      "end": 1039,
      "text": "the more and more we make these mistakes",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u26",
      "start": 1040,
      "end": 1058,
      "text": "when we lose votes",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u27",
      "start": 1059,
      "end": 1087,
      "text": "or demand a recount 10 times",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u28",
      "start": 1088,
      "end": 1148,
      "text": "or let the college vote for the people in the united states.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u29",
      "start": 1149,
      "end": 1185,
      "text": "So witch is it for the Constitution,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u30",
      "start": 1186,
      "end": 1245,
      "text": "are we for Amendment 1 with the freedom of speech and press",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u31",
      "start": 1246,
      "end": 1280,
      "text": "so we can choose our own president",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u32",
      "start": 1281,
      "end": 1332,
      "text": "or is it that we will all go for the 23rd amendment",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u33",
      "start": 1333,
      "end": 1415,
      "text": "and go to letting the few people choose our countries fait for the next four years",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u34",
      "start": 1416,
      "end": 1511,
      "text": "butr then equals the fait for as long as the United States is around free from other countries.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u35",
      "start": 1513,
      "end": 1643,
      "text": "Finally our system of Electoral College is very basis toward whom ever gives them more money to their state or campains more there",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u36",
      "start": 1644,
      "end": 1735,
      "text": "because we all know that the year leading up to the elections are just a popularity contest",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u37",
      "start": 1736,
      "end": 1788,
      "text": "and they just are like trying to get prom king/queen",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u38",
      "start": 1789,
      "end": 1813,
      "text": "everyone promises a vote",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u39",
      "start": 1814,
      "end": 1851,
      "text": "if you give them something in return,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u40",
      "start": 1852,
      "end": 1927,
      "text": "it just happens to be the people who can run for president are very wealthy",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u41",
      "start": 1928,
      "end": 1998,
      "text": "and can afford to give up a small fortune for a for sure vote to them.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u42",
      "start": 1999,
      "end": 2051,
      "text": "But on the other hand if you gave me money like that",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u43",
      "start": 2052,
      "end": 2072,
      "text": "i would vote for you",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u44",
      "start": 2073,
      "end": 2093,
      "text": "if i liked it or not",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u45",
      "start": 2094,
      "end": 2194,
      "text": "and these Electoral College is pressured a little to vote for the person everyone arounf them wants.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u46",
      "start": 2196,
      "end": 2251,
      "text": "If we got rid of the Electoral College system of voting",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u47",
      "start": 2252,
      "end": 2297,
      "text": "i believe that we would have a better economy",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u48",
      "start": 2298,
      "end": 2355,
      "text": "and and the voting system would give more varried results",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u49",
      "start": 2356,
      "end": 2388,
      "text": "so we can get a more acurate way",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u50",
      "start": 2389,
      "end": 2446,
      "text": "because it would be easy to get rid of a system of voting",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u51",
      "start": 2447,
      "end": 2493,
      "text": "but very hard to bring one in to being a thing",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u52",
      "start": 2494,
      "end": 2520,
      "text": "and we can't easly do that",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u53",
      "start": 2521,
      "end": 2560,
      "text": "for the reasons of there is already one",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u54",
      "start": 2561,
      "end": 2615,
      "text": "and that the hoops to jump though for D.C. to pass it.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "u55",
      "start": 2616,
      "end": 2666,
      "text": "therefor i am aginst haviong the Electoral College",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "negative"
    },
    {
      "id": "u56",
      "start": 2667,
      "end": 2709,
      "text": "and bring use Popular Vote for all states.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    }
  ],
